course: dictionary
lesson: 2086
title: Grand words in context
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words and sentences around a hard word. They leave clues about what it means. «Won back by matchless valour, consummate strategy, and a proper handling of sticks.» Valour means bravery and strategy means a clever plan, so the sentence is praising skill. Consummate must be a good quality too.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in. Put «perfect» in place of consummate: «Won back by matchless valour, perfect strategy, and a proper handling of sticks.» It still makes sense, so consummate means perfect or very skilled.
explain: Watch out, because consummate can also mean complete or total, even when the thing is bad. «A consummate liar» is a total liar, not a skilled one. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Consummate is a formal word, so you will meet it in stories and reviews. In The Wind in the Willows, Toad boasts of his own consummate cleverness when he tricks people. The verb has a formal meaning, but you only need to know «complete a deal» for now.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Consummate» means showing very great skill; perfect at something, as in «a consummate musician».
fact: «Consummate» can also mean complete or total, even with a bad quality, as in «a consummate liar».
fact: In exam writing, «consummate» is a strong, formal word for «expert».
fact: The verb «consummate» means to complete or make perfect, as in «to consummate a deal».
exercise: «Won back by matchless valour, consummate strategy, and a proper handling of sticks.» What does consummate mean here? | Tired and sleepy | *Showing great skill; perfect | Loud and noisy | Very old
exercise: Find and copy one word from the sentence that means bravery. | strategy | handling | sticks | *valour
exercise: Ahmed says «a consummate liar» means a bit of a liar. What does consummate mean here? | Slightly, a little | Kind and gentle | Very quiet | *Complete and total
test: «She is a consummate pianist who plays every night.» What does consummate suggest? | Sad and lonely | Hungry | *Great skill, perfect at playing | Very tired
test: In «a consummate fool», what does consummate mean? | Quick at running | *Complete and total | Hungry for food | Thin and tall
exam: In exam writing, which formal word could replace «expert» to sound grand? | cosy | *consummate | silly | tiny
